  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper evaluates CVaR‑VQE for folding 50 peptides of length 7 using a 9‑qubit lattice model and 500,000 shots per run on Amazon Braket simulators. Across the dataset, MD simulation achieved a lower mean interaction energy (2.302 kcal/mol) than VQE (5.885 kcal/mol), although VQE produced negative ground‑state energies for 49 of 50 peptides. The study compares optimization behavior but does not demonstrate computational speedup or quantum advantage.",
